sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Source and data traceability: 72/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "All four primary papers carry DOI and PMID in the docstring, the dataset README and the .bib; the upstream repository and its derivation chain are named with a full commit hash and MIT notice; the three JSON fixtures are SHA-256 pinned in the script and in datasets/bressloff/README.md with their upstream paths, and both GitHub URLs resolve. -8: the Rule et al. 2011 PMID differs between the script (21980279) and paper_citations.bib (21980269), so at least one identifier is wrong. -5: the .bib gives year = 2001 for Ermentrout & Cowan 1979. -8: the Floquet fixture's source_curve_comparison points to an upstream reports/source-curves file that is not vendored, so the digitised Fig. 8 curves the panel implicitly claims to reproduce cannot be inspected. -7: the retino-cortical constants alpha = 3/pi, beta = 1.589/2, w0 = 0.087, eps = 0.051 and the \"Eq. 3.12 / Eq. 4.9\" equation numbers are asserted without page or equation references that can be checked, and 11 of the 24 upstream runs carry status \"review\"/\"phase-selection-review\" that the script does not surface. Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L11–L31: DOIs, PMIDs and pinned upstream commit 344863a1 in docstring <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L11-L31>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L74–L78: SHA-256 pins for the three vendored fixtures, verified at run time and fail-closed <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L74-L78>; datasets/bressloff/paper_citations.bib L36–L54: Ermentrout & Cowan year=2001; Rule 2011 pmid=21980269 vs script's 21980279 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/datasets/bressloff/paper_citations.bib#L36-L54>; datasets/bressloff/README.md L9–L13: fixture table with SHA-256 and upstream paths; source-curves file referenced by rule-2011-floquet.json not vendored <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/datasets/bressloff/README.md#L9-L13>." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-source-traceability> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.72"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-source-traceability> rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants (2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py, docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif, bressloff_v1_metrics.csv) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Source and data traceability' for Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes" ;
        dcterms:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (primary) + Gemini 4 Argon (independent blinded second assessor)" .
}

